A thread's watch is a root of the derivation tree rather than a node below the capability it was set with,
so no revoke above it clears it, and the destroy of the notification's pool leaves it naming freed memory.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: capability to an object is a root

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -427,7 +427,7 @@ static int op_thread(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, const
         if (bits != 0) {
             /* It hangs below the capability it was set with, so a revoke above that clears it. */
             target->watch = (struct cap){ .type = CAP_WATCHED, .rights = nc.rights, .a = nc.a, .b = bits };
-            cap_attach(slot_node(t, arg[1]), &target->watch);
+            cap_attach(NULL, &target->watch);
         }
         return KERR_OK;
     }
